          "source_text_sha256": "e5452126be96afc455c4624d5283a2b1264d82cef72c5fe5d4370aa169f23d1d",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: During a fair on October 27, 2013, a witness observed and photographed a black object moving very slowly under the clouds. Several people then observed the phenomenon, but only one testimony was collected. The witness described the object as: a black to gray, oval object that changes shape, resembling a complexly shaped balloon turning with the wind. Due to it being observed against a clear sky, it appears extremely dark, regardless of its actual color. The wind at Luc-Cannet des Maures (Source: Meteociel) was variable, light, changing from East in the morning, North at noon, and West in late afternoon; this is not entirely consistent with the observed movement, but it is extremely difficult to estimate wind in a mountainous area with light winds. Despite this uncertainty, given the similarity of the object to a balloon, likely related to a local festival, the GEIPAN classifies this case as \"unremarkable\" category \"B\": probable observation of an helium-filled festive balloon.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "80981b0b45a06ea1b952ab215d0fad5e7b9dbecda13a9c195dbb1ad3ee6ada7f"
        }
